5. Synthesis
   Egyptian fractions and n=16 LRC share the same hidden question:
     can reciprocal mass be split without leaving a residue?
   For k/N = 1/b + 1/c the residue is a divisor congruence
     d | N^2, d == -N mod k.
   For an LRC endpoint, the residue is an inequality
     |p*(16m+eps) - 16*a*u| < u.
   The S394 q-counterterm is the finite-part version of the same
   move: replace an infinite reciprocal object by a finite triangular
   one and keep track of the anti-reciprocal defect x-1/x.

   Creative n=16 proof angle:
     prove that any all-protected endpoint system with a 16-gate
     induces an Egyptian split ledger across dyadic layers; the
     unsplit residues must be paid by even breaker speeds, and those
     breakers create a q-like negative counterterm visible as a
     positive LRC gap or a private endpoint leaf.
